menu "SIP Phone"

    config SIP_PHONE_WIFI_SSID
        string "First-boot Wi-Fi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            SSID written to NVS the first time the device boots with no stored
            configuration. Leave empty to provision later through the web UI
            (once it exists) or by flashing a config. Changing this value does
            not alter an NVS configuration that has already been created.
            Never commit real credentials to a shared sdkconfig.defaults.

    config SIP_PHONE_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "First-boot Wi-Fi password"
        default ""
        help
            Password stored in plain text in NVS alongside the SSID. Leave empty
            for an open network. Enable NVS encryption before deploying.

    choice SIP_PHONE_AUDIO_BACKEND
        prompt "Audio hardware"
        default SIP_PHONE_AUDIO_INMP441
        help
            Selects which audio driver is compiled. Only one backend can own
            the I2S peripherals, and the XIAO wiring is invalid on this board.

        config SIP_PHONE_AUDIO_NONE
            bool "No audio backend"
            help
                No microphone or speaker driver is created. Calls still set up
                and tear down over SIP but carry no audio. Use this for board
                bring-up before the audio hardware is wired.

        config SIP_PHONE_AUDIO_XIAO_PDM
            bool "XIAO PDM mic + I2S speaker (41/42, 7/8/9)"
            help
                The original XIAO ESP32-S3 Sense wiring. Do not enable this on
                the JC4827W543: GPIO8 is the GT911 SDA and GPIO41/42 drive the
                onboard amplifier.

        config SIP_PHONE_AUDIO_INMP441
            bool "INMP441 mic + onboard I2S amplifier (6/7/15, 42/2/41)"
            help
                JC4827W543 backend. INMP441 SCK/WS/SD on GPIO6/7/15 with L/R
                tied to ground; amplifier BCLK/LRC/DOUT on GPIO42/2/41. The
                amplifier pins come from the project brief and are not yet
                confirmed against the board schematic.
    endchoice

    config SIP_PHONE_LEGACY_BUTTONS
        bool "Enable the XIAO ANSWER/HANGUP buttons"
        default n
        help
            The original buttons used GPIO3 (ANSWER) and GPIO2 (HANGUP). On
            the JC4827W543 GPIO3 is the GT911 interrupt line, so the touch UI
            replaces them.

endmenu
